  "platform": "Sega Mega Drive / Genesis",
  "summary": "Rocket Knight Adventures is Konami's platform action game, first released for Mega Drive in Japan on 6 August 1993.",
  "body": [
    "Rocket Knight Adventures is Konami's platform action game, first released for Mega Drive in Japan on 6 August 1993. Sparkster, an armoured opossum with a sword and rocket pack, fights the invading Devotindos Empire. His journey moves through castles, machinery and airborne battles, repeatedly changing the setting and the task placed in front of him. Nobuya Nakazato directed the game after working on Contra. Its seven stages use Sparkster's unusual equipment to connect ordinary platforming with short bursts of flight and large, staged confrontations.",
    "The sword supplies an immediate attack, while charging the rocket pack prepares a powerful dash. Choosing a direction before releasing that charge sends Sparkster through the air, making the same action useful for crossing a gap and striking an enemy. The pause required to charge gives movement a distinct rhythm: find a safe position, judge the route, then commit. Stage layouts place walls, platforms and threats around that ability, so learning where a burst will end matters as much as knowing when to begin it.",
    "The adventure repeatedly interrupts its platforming with another kind of encounter, including scrolling flight and battles against large machines. Those changes introduce fresh situations while keeping the sword and rocket pack at the centre of the action. Animated reactions and mechanical enemies give the conflict a comic energy, with Sparkster's small figure facing devices that fill much of the screen. The soundtrack includes work by Michiru Yamane and other Konami composers. Together, the varied staging and consistent movement system give the journey a strong sense of momentum from one set piece to the next."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "A knight with a rocket pack",
    "Charging the next move",
    "An adventure that keeps changing"
  ],
